# Replace abrahamFerga with the GitHub login read from workflow.json or `gh api user` — never a hardcoded
# name, or this file works for exactly one account.
#
# CODEOWNERS is the human-visibility half of the spine policy: it puts a named person on the review
# of anything touching the five guarantees the platform exists to provide. The ENFORCING half is
# `pr-gates.mjs`, which requires a live, uncontradicted agent verdict for a protected diff.
# CODEOWNERS only requests visibility; do not turn on "Require review from Code Owners" when the
# scheduled merger is enabled, because that converts the queue back to manual merging.
#
# Keep both. The check is what verifies the agent verdict; the ownership is what tells you it happened.

* @abrahamFerga

# The spine — RBAC before the model, approval-first writes, tenant isolation, audit, secrets.
/src/**/Authorization/     @abrahamFerga
/src/**/Approvals/         @abrahamFerga
/src/**/Persistence/       @abrahamFerga

# The harness itself. An agent that can edit its own gates has no gates.
/.github/                  @abrahamFerga
/CODEOWNERS                @abrahamFerga
/nuget.config              @abrahamFerga
/workflow.json             @abrahamFerga
